/inputs/2\",\"/inputs/3\",\"/inputs/4\"]},\"argument\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The local support/continuity reasoning and the stated M001/M011 integration-by-parts route support the spatial calculation, conditional on the inputs. But the final step claiming E′(r)=∫e_t is not justified: differentiating the integral requires a differentiation-under-the-integral argument/theorem, and S001 neither proves it nor has such an input. N002's facts do not assert that identity. This is the first unsupported implication.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inputs/1/statement\",\"/output/statement\"]},\"dependency_accounting\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The listed inputs have identifiable roles in integrability, integration by parts and the Haar-measure identification. However, the final differentiation/interchange uses a substantive result not listed or proved locally; the finite-dimensional calculation policy cannot supply it.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/inputs\",\"/logic/calculations\"]},\"output\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The desired formula is the stated output, and the proof reaches the formal expression involving ∫e_t. It does not establish that this expression equals E′(r), so it fails to derive the output.\",\"locations\":[\"/output/statement\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\"]},\"scope\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The arbitrary r is introduced for the universal conclusion, and the prose states the result for arbitrary r>0. No temporary assumption or witness is used to escape its scope. This does not cure the missing differentiation argument.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/locals/0\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/output/binders\"]},\"applicability\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"On the conditional packet premises, M001's compact-support integrability application is matched to the three continuous compactly supported scalar functions; M011 is instantiated with the stated Euclidean spaces, inner product and direction, with integrability and smooth derivative conditions; M017 supplies the Haar-measure fact for Fin n. This checks the packet's application mappings only, not source fidelity.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs/2/source_contract\",\"/inputs/3/source_contract\",\"/inputs/4/source_contract\",\"/inference/applications/0\",\"/inference/applications/1\",\"/inference/applications/2\"]},\"statement_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The packet supplies complete input and output statements and their referenced definitions. N003 states the quantified energy-derivative formula; the remaining failure is proof sufficiency, not inability to read the target statement.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs/0/statement\",\"/inputs/1/statement\",\"/output/statement\",\"/definitions/0\",\"/definitions/1\",\"/definitions/2\",\"/definitions/3\"]},\"object_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The actual objects used in S001 are accounted for by frozen parameters, definitions, input-bound quantities or the local declarations for r, j, v_j, f_j and g. The local definitions are introduced before their substantive use in the prose. No missing witness is needed for the failure identified.\",\"locations\":[\"/parameters\",\"/definitions\",\"/inference/locals\",\"/inference/argument/0/objects\"]},\"dependency_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The factual uses of N001/N002 and the M inputs are identifiable, but the assertion that N002 identifies E′(r)=∫e_t is not a fact in N002 and is not derived in the inference. The missing differentiation-under-the-integral justification is an unlisted dependency/local proof.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs/1/statement\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/inputs\"]},\"packet_replay\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"This review used packet.json as its sole task-mathematical material, plus the declared procedural rules; no other mathematical task material or source proof was read. On that packet alone, the replayed argument is insufficient at the final differentiation-under-the-integral step, so packet_replay does not pass mathematical sufficiency. No runtime/carrier attestation is claimed here; identity, canonical hash binding and transmitted-material readback are outside this review.\",\"locations\":[\"/packet_sha256\",\"/warning\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inputs/1/statement\"]}},\"findings\":[{\"location\":\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"finding\":\"First unsupported implication: “N002 identifies E′(r)=∫e_t.” N002 states integrability of e(·,t), and a time window with continuity and common compact support properties for e and e_t; it does not state the derivative-of-integral identity. The argument supplies no proof of differentiation under the integral sign, and no declared input provides it. Therefore E′(r)=∫e_t, and hence the requested output, is unsupported.\"}]}}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read an explicitly frozen task document by ID; no other local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"st